      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-11-10">Published November 10, 2026</time></p>

      <p>PocketBook's second-generation large-format color e-note is official. The <strong>PocketBook InkPad Eo 2</strong> — a 10.3-inch color E Ink tablet running a fully open Android 14 with Google Play access — launched in September 2026, and the first hands-on hardware impressions landed this week. For anyone who reads EPUBs, annotates PDFs, or wants a distraction-free note-taking slab that is not locked to one store, this is the most interesting non-Amazon large-screen release of the fall.</p>

      <p>This article is a specs-and-positioning first look based on PocketBook's published hardware details and the earliest review units. We cover the display, the stylus stack, the format support that makes it EPUB-relevant, and who this device is actually for.</p>

      <h2>Hardware at a Glance</h2>

      <p>The InkPad Eo 2 is a premium 10.3-inch color e-note, not a casual reader. PocketBook is targeting the same productivity niche as the reMarkable Paper Pro and the Onyx Boox Note Air series, but with a different software philosophy: full Android instead of a locked or semi-locked OS.</p>

